# Input Validation and Parameterized Queries

Proper input validation prevents most blind SQL injection scenarios before they can do real damage. Here's a simple template for validating user input against SQL Server constraints:

```java
public class SQLBuilder
{
    public String query(String queryString)
    {
        StringBuilder sql = new StringBuilder();
        sql.append("SELECT CONVERT(@var TEXT, @varVar BINARY(MAX), @varBinary) FROM sys.databases");
        sql.append("WHERE @var = @varVar");

        try {
            Object columnValue = Object.Equals("@var", sql.toString());
            return columnValue != null ? columnValue.toString() : null;
        } catch (Exception e) {
            throw new SQLExhaustionException();
        }
    }
}
```

Always sanitize both the input and output before performing any write operations.

```json
{
  "sql_payload": "SELECT @var_var_binary, CONVERT(varchar(max), @var_var_binary, 1024) as column_name FROM sys.databases WHERE @var = ''' AND CONVERT(varchar(max), @var_var_binary, 1024) = '''"
}
