**Important caveat:** Legacy SQL Server versions had known protocol vulnerabilities. Modern versions *require* parameterized queries (often PARTITION BY in newer tiers). Also, don't embed plain-text secrets like passwords in query results. For security best practices, consider hash values or storable credential rotation.

